@@ -0,0 +1,14 @@
+# Full independent review request
+
+Proposed disposition: original unresolved, five substantive author turns exhausted. Review the entire source/proof packet before treating any scoped result as accepted. FINAL_AUTHOR_MANIFEST.json binds the complete public packet; older manifests bind historical checkpoints and are preserved.
+
+Read SOURCE_SCOPE.md, RESULT.md and TURN_1.md through TURN_5.md. Particular risks:
+
+- The exact split Green ring, complex analytical scalar field, dimension-weighted completion, duality and universal symmetry quantifier; do not substitute a stable quotient or a C*-completion.
+- Turn1: descent of decomposition/isomorphism data over arbitrary algebraic extensions, norm preservation, spectral-radius use, countable tensor closure and the logical direction of compactness.
+- Turn2: actual independent endotrivial cores, credited gamma input, all bounded characters, p-group projective splitting and the fact that the coordinate dimension functional on the stable quotient is not multiplicative.
+- Turn3: quaternion presentation, matrix handedness, exact ranks and all-field characteristic-two extension, minimality and exact stable period, nonzero Fourier idempotents, full/stable spectral computation and the restriction cancellation. The example is a failed restriction bound, not nonsymmetry.
+- Turn4: every abstract axiom, dimension character, all Fourier characters and the separate actual-group nonrealizability argument. An abstract counterexample cannot settle the original universal group question.
+- Turn5: local tensor endomorphism ring over arbitrary k; distinct subgroup detection and distinct class recovery; actual Green-coordinate injection; tensor normalization and projective removal; Möbius signs; the lower and upper bounds and onto argument for completed blocks; bounded inverse of the finite product decomposition; explicit proper-family F8 module. Do not infer symmetry of the whole Green completion from this proper subalgebra.
+
+Run python replay_author.py. The turn5 auxiliary finite group functor is expressly a structural control and is not asserted to be T(H). Check the primary PDFs against SOURCE_MANIFEST.json and SOURCE_ADDITION_T3.json if the local source directory is available. Do not count new review controls or additive corrections as another author turn.
