+# Substantive author turn 3
+
+This turn tested the extension of elementary-abelian positive-growth detection to full spectral data. It constructs an actual rational self-adjoint virtual Q8-module whose restriction to every elementary abelian subgroup vanishes, while its full-completion spectrum is {0,-2,-4}. The classical quaternion resolution is credited to Langer and verified by explicit group-ring composites and four GF(2) minor certificates. Periodicity reduces the infinite resolution assertion to those exact finite checks.
+
+The spectrum is real, so this is a failed-proof-route obstruction, not a counterexample to symmetry. It shows that invisible restriction directions cannot simply be dismissed as radical. The checker contains 746 exact assertions with the determinant certificates recorded. Author count: 3/5.
